// @error print expects a value, got void
// CONTRACT (must-error): `print` demands a value to render, and a void call has none.
// The demanded type here comes from INFERENCE — there is no written type for the
// assignability rules to compare the argument against, so the messages that cover the
// annotated slots (`cannot assign void to 'x' of type i32`, `argument 1: expected i32, got
// void`) never fire on this position. Left unrefused the void reached codegen, whose print
// ladder ends in `call __print_i32__` with nothing on the stack: `vl check` reported the
// program clean and the emitted module failed to validate.
//
// A VERDICT pin, deliberately: the defect is that the program does not build, so there is
// no run to compare a `@log` against. The fix makes it fail EARLIER (check instead of
// validation), which only a verdict can express.
function pv() { print(1) }
print(pv())
